Title: Upstream fixes: draft KV out of checkpoints, pinned host buffers
Add-on: cherry-picks of two open upstream pull requests, exactly as proposed there; drop this patch when they are merged.
  ggml-org/llama.cpp#29509: the draft (MTP) KV is not stored in the context checkpoints (it is a prefix-addressed cache that stays resident, and it made every checkpoint grow with the context).
  ggml-org/llama.cpp#30449: the pinned host buffer type of CUDA has a 4 GiB maximum size, so a large set of CPU-resident expert weights (--load-mode none) is split into several
  pinned buffers instead of one allocation that fails on Windows and silently falls back to pageable memory (which makes the expert uploads of --moe-cache-mib much slower).

diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index e95fb63ab3cc..e9727aaf4259 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -2361,7 +2361,7 @@ struct server_context_impl {
         cur.update_pos(slot.prompt.n_tokens() - n_tokens_cur, pos_min, pos_max);
 
         cur.update_tgt(ctx_tgt, slot.id, LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_FLAGS_PARTIAL_ONLY);
-        cur.update_dft(ctx_dft, slot.id, LLAMA_STATE_SEQ_FLAGS_PARTIAL_ONLY);
+
         // stash the draft's speculative state with the checkpoint
         common_speculative_get_state(spec.get(), slot.id, cur.data_spec);
 
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
